# Cloudflare Pages response headers (copied to dist/ by Vite).
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is REPORT-ONLY on purpose. Deploy it, use the
# site (log in, open a gardener page, upload a photo, open it inside the
# Telegram Mini App) with the browser console open, and look for
# "Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only" warnings. When there are none, rename
# the header to Content-Security-Policy to enforce it.
#
# Why it matters: the session token sits in localStorage, bound to a device
# key. The key stops a *copied* token from working elsewhere, but script
# running inside the page can still ask the browser to sign requests. A CSP
# that only allows our own scripts (plus Telegram's SDK) is what keeps
# injected script out.
#
# Allowed on purpose:
#   telegram.org                    the Mini App SDK <script> in index.html
#   static.cloudflareinsights.com   Cloudflare Pages web analytics beacon
#   api.kochatim.uz                 the API (fetch) and its image proxy (<img>)
#   *.ibb.co                        ImgBB, where uploaded photos live
#   images.unsplash.com             the picture on the landing page
#   frame-ancestors telegram        the Mini App is embedded by Telegram clients
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'       React sets style="" attributes
/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://telegram.org https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.kochatim.uz https://*.ibb.co https://images.unsplash.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.kochatim.uz https://cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self' data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self' https://web.telegram.org https://*.telegram.org
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
